I would  encourage you to consume meals and  snacks which are high in complex carbs  such as whole-grain bread potato brown  rice bananas beans other fruits and  vegetables have them for breakfast  because these high-fiber foods will take  much longer for your body to digest  hence it will help to control cravings  throughout the day and if you have  complex carbs on an empty stomach it  will have to increase serotonin levels  within an hour so  no more graphic days ahead sugar  cravings when your blood sugar level is  low you crave for sweets and so you have  it this will then increase your blood  sugar level but only for a short while  you will end up wanting more sugary food  and drinks and that is why some of us  can be addicted to sugars have you  experienced this before to break this  cycle go for food that contains natural  sugars such as fruits juices honey  yogurt and carbs consuming these foods  with complex carbs will help you to  balance your blood sugar level and to  reduce cravings if you're someone that  experienced magnesium and iron  deficiency while the good news is you  can give in to your chocolate cravings  chocolates are high in magnesium and  iron but also high in fat so try to  choose high-quality antioxidant rich  dark chocolate over milk chocolate which  typically has more calories and fat or  you can have a cup of hot chocolate and  remember to consume in moderation other  high iron and magnesium foods include  beans seeds nuts green vegetables fish  and red meat so if you are looking for  an excuse to consume red meat this is  the perfect time a nice lean piece of  red meat can help to increase iron and  also to make up for what's lost each  month magnesium can also have to  decrease common Mastro symptoms such as  blue  ting constipation headaches anxiety or  swollen breasts so do increase your  magnesium and iron intakes tip for  calcium calcium has been shown to help  with PMS a woman who has a diet high in  calcium tend to experience 